%% Accepted (owner, 2026-11-15), design only; not implemented. Owner: Governance. Axis: client_registrations.status_id (app_zenith).
%% Source: adr/sign-up-finalization-in-auth.md, Cosmos split amendment. Not implemented.
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> CREDENTIAL_PENDING: start (H1 accepted - eligibility and requirements cleared except one Auth credential)
    [*] --> COMPLETED: start and complete in one transaction (H1 - method needs no Auth credential)
    CREDENTIAL_PENDING --> COMPLETED: complete (H3 accepted - account rows, receipt and jti in one app_zenith transaction)
    CREDENTIAL_PENDING --> CANCELLED: cancel (H5 accepted - cookie and cer match)
    CREDENTIAL_PENDING --> EXPIRED: expire (deadline_at passed on database clock - request time or sweep)
    CREDENTIAL_PENDING --> HALTED: halt (superseded_by_identifier, superseded_in_browser, identifier_taken, integrity_violation)
    COMPLETED --> [*]
    CANCELLED --> [*]
    EXPIRED --> [*]
    HALTED --> [*]

    note right of CREDENTIAL_PENDING
        Holds the identifier claim and the WebAuthn user handle reservation.
        At most one per identifier and one per browser (partial unique indexes).
        No Client, contact, external identity or passkey row exists yet.
        A rejected credential, conflict or replay leaves this state unchanged.
    end note
    note right of COMPLETED
        Terminal states are absorbing. Physical purge after purge_after is
        deletion, not a state. Chronicle audit events survive the purge.
    end note
